# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, three kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.
# Plan 00167 (#90): builds cc-project-dir beside cc and installs the new cc, which starts at the
# top of a git repository and, typed outside one, offers this checkout [Y/n] (refusing on no,
# or with no terminal). ccy stays at 3.99.12.18, already installed. Afterwards type cc in ~
# twice (accept once, decline once) and once in a project subfolder.
# Plan 00135 Task 10.1 (#86): it also rebuilds ccy-sessions, whose verify-restore now reports a
# session sitting at Claude Code's conversation picker as WAITING-AT-PROMPT thread-picker, not
# OK, so fedora-desktop-self-update verify fails on it.
playbooks/imports/play-claude-yolo.yml
# Plan 00194 Tasks 2.0b, 2.0h and 2.0i: the goodbye host checks, automated (acceptance.bash; the
# plan has no triage.bash or deploy.bash), run again for G3 (window closed). The last run passed
# G1 (Ctrl-C) and G2 (podman stop); in G3 the launcher now stops the container and runs the
# disconnect notice (Task 2.0h, deployed), but pingbus dropped it as a duplicate of G2's notice
# sent 19 s earlier (Task 2.0i, to be fixed and queued above this entry). G3 keeps the launcher's
# stderr and the checkout's disconnect.log as evidence. The whole script runs again, so G1 and
# G2 are repeated. It makes two throwaway teams,
# starts three idle ccy sessions on them in a scratch checkout on its own tmux server, ends one
# with Ctrl-C, one with podman stop and one by closing its window, counts the goodbye and
# disconnected messages each team gets, then removes all of it. No SSH key or agent goes into
# the sessions. Each launch runs ccy's normal startup clean-up, which removes every exited or
# created ccy container on the host (as any ccy launch does). The team purge relies on sudo
# staying cached (it does on this host). One sudo prompt.
00194-agent-bus-live-delivery-supervisor-plugin
# Plan 00187 (#100): builds and installs wsi and deploys wsi-stream (restarting the warm
# speech server) and the panel extension, so that while Claude post-processes a Ctrl+Insert
# dictation the panel icon is 🤖, and 💬 for Alt+Insert, instead of the orange loading icon;
# Insert during it flashes the no-entry sign. The extension changed: LOG OUT and back in
# before it shows. Then look: dictate with Ctrl+Insert, then Alt+Insert, and watch the icon
# after the orange loading icon (the debug log says "Display: CLAUDE_PROCESSING").
playbooks/imports/optional/common/play-speech-to-text.yml
# Plan 00183 Task 2.2 (#52): re-runs the basic configs play, which now imports play-golang.yml
# (golang is already installed, so no change there), builds git-fetch-age from src-go and
# installs it root-owned as /usr/local/bin/git-fetch-age, then deploys the new
# /var/local/ps1-prompt. New shells then show a yellow [fetched 14d ago] beside the directory
# in a checkout whose last fetch is an hour old or more. It never fetches. Open terminals keep
# the old prompt until a new shell is started. Asks for the PS1 colour only if none is set.
playbooks/imports/play-basic-configs.yml
